# {{GAME}} — Unity + UniSpring

Instructions for every coding agent working on this project (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor,
Copilot and others). The full rules are the `unispring-game-dev` skill
(`{{SKILL_DIR}}/SKILL.md`, Agent Skills format): load it before any change under `Assets/`
and when designing a subsystem. Project settings for the checks: `unispring-skill.json`.

## Invariants

1. **The only editable zone is `Assets/Src/`.** `Packages/`, `ProjectSettings/`,
   `Assets/Settings/` and vendor folders are read-only without explicit permission.
   Move assets together with their `.meta`; never change GUIDs.
2. **Modules talk only through `*.Api`.** No references to another module's
   `Internal`/`Runtime`, services, DAOs or ports. `public` ≠ "available to other modules".
   Module assemblies: `{{PREFIX}}.<Module>.Api` / `.Runtime` / `.Presentation` / `.Editor` / `.Tests`.
   Layers inside a module: `{{SKILL_DIR}}/references/layers.md`.
3. **DI is UniSpring** (`com.ialex86.unispring`; configuration —
   `Assets/Src/Scripts/Bootstrap/UniSpringConfiguration.cs`). Services: `[Service]` +
   constructor injection of interfaces. MonoBehaviours: `AutowiredMonoBehaviour`,
   `[Autowired]` fields, `OnDependenciesInjected()`, **never declare `Awake`**. No `new`
   for services, singletons, `Find*` or Service Locator. Saves — `[Repository]` + mapper +
   validator, transactions — `[Transactional]`, notifications — `IEventPublisher`,
   per-frame logic — `ITickable`/`ILifecycle`, tables — `[ConfigurationProperties]`.
4. **No `switch` / `else` / `else if` in new code.** Choose behaviour with
   `[Strategy]` + `IKeyedStrategy<TKey>` + `StrategyRegistry`. `if` only as a guard clause.
5. **Logging only through `UniSpring.Logging.GameLog`.** No `Debug.Log*`, `Console.Write*`,
   `print`. Never pass the `caller` argument.
6. **Player-facing text only from language tables** (`Assets/Src/Resources/Localization/<lang>.json`;
   keys in code, every key in every table, no unused keys).
7. **Read the actual API first** (UniSpring in `Library/PackageCache`, neighbours' asmdefs).
8. **Don't fix unrelated legacy violations** and **don't commit or push** unless asked.

## Source of truth

Current code lives only in `Assets/Src/`. When documentation disagrees with code, trust the
code and report it. Subsystem docs: `Assets/Src/Doc/<Module>/README.md`.

## Checks

Before reporting a change as done, run the gate — it fails only on violations the change
added (legacy is listed in the committed `unispring-baseline.json`) and on any
localization problem:

```bash
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/gate.py check --root .
```

The same gate runs in the git pre-commit hook and in CI. Never bypass it (`--no-verify`)
and never grow the baseline to hide new code; shrink it with `gate.py baseline` after
fixing legacy. Plus the Unity compile and EditMode/PlayMode tests of the touched modules
(fast run: without `Slow`). A new `.cs` without a `.meta` is flagged until Unity imports it.
New module: `python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/new-module.py --root . --name <Module> [--presentation]`.

## Review

Before reporting a change under `Assets/` as done (and before a commit), have the diff
reviewed independently: `{{SKILL_DIR}}/references/review.md` says how in each agent, and
what the reviewer checks. Fix confirmed findings or explain why they don't apply.

## Several agents in one Unity

Unity MCP is connected in each client's own settings; the repository's MCP config stays
empty. Change the project through Unity MCP **only while holding the lease**; calls go
through `execute_code` with `compiler: "codedom"`:

```csharp
return {{NAMESPACE}}.AgentLease.Editor.EditorLease.Acquire("<short-session-name>", "<what I'm doing>");
return {{NAMESPACE}}.AgentLease.Editor.EditorLease.Renew("<token>");
return {{NAMESPACE}}.AgentLease.Editor.EditorLease.Release("<token>");
return {{NAMESPACE}}.AgentLease.Editor.EditorLease.Status();
```

`BUSY` — work without Unity and check later; never release someone else's lease. Read-only
calls need no lease. Release the lease before your reply ends. Details:
`{{SKILL_DIR}}/references/agent-workflow.md`.
